cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Handy: real-time few-shot sign language recognition"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Taue
    given-names: Yota
    affiliation: "Nakazawa-Ohkoshi Laboratory, Faculty of Policy Management, Keio University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yoyo222/handy-slr"
abstract: >-
  Handy recognises sign language in real time from MediaPipe hand landmarks,
  embedding motion into a 256-dimensional metric space with a CNN+TCN encoder and
  matching against stored prototypes with partial dynamic time warping. New signs
  are registered from two recordings without retraining. This repository also
  contains a class-disjoint few-shot evaluation of the method on WLASL, covering a
  hand-detection fallback, DBA prototype aggregation, a batched Soft-DTW loss, a
  continuous-stream benchmark, and conformal calibration of the rejection
  threshold.
keywords:
  - sign language recognition
  - few-shot learning
  - dynamic time warping
  - metric learning
  - MediaPipe
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"
